WEBVTT

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:14.240
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.410
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:26.960
I was prepared for the time you left

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.800
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:40.310
After I embraced you with all I had

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:49.860
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.530
filled my heart

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:00.040
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:06.710
You gave me happiness

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.050
Until I meet you again one day

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.550
Until I know what you are truly like

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.090
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.800
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.890
I won't forget your smile

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.240
Where did

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.530
my face go?

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.540
Come on. You'd better get changed.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.460
What are these clothes?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.460
I know it isn't your style, but you should practice a little.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.550
It's no good if you can't manage this kind of thing by yourself.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.470
M-M-Manager?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.720
That's right.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.390
You're supposed to be the manager, so manage.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.890
No, I don't mean me...

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.270
There's a lot I'm still not able to wrap my head around...

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.610
You can say that again.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.230
Even though you're still young...

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.240
<b>Hazuki Family Ceremony</b>

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.260
Wait a second...

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.260
Look...

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.890
Why the hell am I sleeping?!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.060
Hey, wake up!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.980
Seriously, what are you doing to me?!

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.780
When did this happen?!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.740
You really are dense, aren't you?

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.200
After being here so long,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.200
what made you think you could go back?

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.500
The moment you got too involved with something that wasn't human,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.920
it was like you were fated to be sacrificed.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.170
You weren't properly mentally prepared...

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.050
There was something naive nagging at you in the back of your mind.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.010
This is your fate.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.680
Accept it.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.570
You...

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.990
You're just saying that again.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:46.820
You're so naive.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.410
You ruined your whole life by being head over heels in love.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.000
Moreover, you're just a beginner.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.540
You have no right to say that to me.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.540
Just how much do you love that girl?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.300
What are you—

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.170
A young guy like you who shows up out of the blue...

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.050
Nobody...

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.550
Nobody could ever...

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:14.890
Hey.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.400
Don't tell me <i>you</i> are that stupid husband?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.770
Don't be so rough with Rokka.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.110
Then show me your real face.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.320
Fine.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.320
Can I hit you?

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.120
As boorish as ever...

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:32.990
<b>Hazuki Family Grave</b>

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.370
Being like that is the reason you're going to take my place six feet under.
<b>Hazuki Family Grave</b>

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.120
<b>Hazuki Family Grave</b>

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.130
Just so you know,

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.380
I'm the author of this book.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.760
Everything is just as I imagine it.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.470
Stop screwing around and give me back my body right now!

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.140
You first.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.440
Give Rokka back to me.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.400
What do you mean, "give her back?"

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.990
The manager doesn't belong to me.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.780
Give her back.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.490
She's not a thing!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:11.450
I'm asking you.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.410
Then I'll ask you for a favor, too.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.330
Set her free already!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.120
I can't.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.210
Without a second thought...

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.710
I don't want you to have anything more to do with my wife and me.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.970
Don't wrap her up in your ego.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.260
I think you'll come to realize it if you die,

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.350
just like I did.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.440
It's inconceivable while you're alive.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.060
But like me, you should learn that the feeling of not being able to handle something

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.480
becomes overblown when you're dead.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.400
As long as you've got a physical body, rationality wins out.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.950
But right now,

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.120
even you don't...

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:56.740
Right?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.000
You've...

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.170
got it all figured out for yourself,

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.130
but what's gonna happen to the manager?

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.000
Only a married couple can understand a married couple.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.260
This late in the day, I don't expect you to understand anything.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.470
Are those the words of a person who's asking for a favor?

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.110
What is this situation?

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.690
A suspenseful play?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.650
Are you prepared to dive into the sea?

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.530
I can't remember doing anything to deserve someone's ill will!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.540
What are you talking about?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.300
You did everything you could to make me hate you.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.470
And so,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.430
I'll be taking care of the rest.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.430
Hey, don't do this!

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.430
Goodnight.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.610
<i>Idiot...</i>

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.250
Look.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.000
They built a giant tower.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.470
I never imagined we'd be able to see it together.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.090
We have to be grateful to Hazuki.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.560
Right, Shimao?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.430
That we do, Rokka.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.190
<i>You're satisfied with that?</i>

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:54.490
<i>I mean, is that your answer?</i>

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.370
<i>So in the end,</i>

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.540
<i>in exchange for my life,</i>

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.290
<i>I came here to be unceremoniously dumped?</i>

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.130
All too soon...

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.510
That's why you were shut up in here in the end.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:30.520
"Tragedy becomes a beautiful, foolish young man,"

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.820
Thumbelina thought.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.780
The end.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:53.640
<i>Is this a dream I'm having in his nonsensical book?</i>

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:57.600
<i>Although the scenery is different than it's been so far...</i>

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.320
<i>This is certainly a significant thing to leave behind.</i>

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.340
<i>An ill-omened dream...</i>

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.430
<i>That was a nasty hint.</i>

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:30.850
<i>Anyway, I can't let myself get confounded here.</i>

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:35.350
You might mistakenly step into a grave and not even notice it.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.730
<i>Gotta get it together.</i>

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.780
<i>Can't die before my parents,</i>

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.820
<i>let alone die without noticing it.</i>

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:52.870
<i>It's not like I was born to sacrifice myself for that self-centered ghost.</i>

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:57.910
<i>From here on out, my plan is to learn the trade,</i>

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.630
<i>reassure the manager, and live the hell out of life for my own sake.</i>

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.590
<i>That's what I'm laying the foundation for.</i>

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:24.070
I'm sorry for crying.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.540
A moving scene like this, and you...

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.460
You too, Shimao!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:47.960
I've got rice balls.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:49.670
Really?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:52.220
Did you put the stuff I like in them?

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.260
Salty bonito.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.980
Of course I put that in!

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.280
Crying, laughing...

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.990
Today's a busy day, isn't it?

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:19.500
It seems you're being more open with me than before, Rokka.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:24.000
I think the last memory I have of you crying

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.630
was while watching a movie when we were still students.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.260
It was the third in a late night marathon.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.430
You have a good memory.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.340
Goes to show how rare it is for you.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.770
<i>In the end,</i>

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.600
<i>I wasn't able to get her to depend on me.</i>

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.900
Here you are.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.280
Thank you.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.120
<i>That's definitely my dream.</i>

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.040
<i>Being with the manager after her wish has come true.</i>

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.040
<i>I've missed her so much.</i>

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.550
<i>I love that round head.</i>

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.050
<i>So cute.</i>

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.050
Shimao...

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:22.560
You like processed fish, like dried bonito and tuna, huh?

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.100
Yeah.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.600
Canned salmon, too.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.810
<i>What is he doing here?</i>

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:31.320
<i>Wait a second. Something's...</i>

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.070
<i>That's... me?</i>

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.500
<i>What are those glasses?</i>

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.290
<i>What's with that haircut?!</i>

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.540
<i>In my own dream, I'm wearing a weird get-up</i>

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.130
<i>and sitting next to the manager as she calls me "Shimao."</i>

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.920
<i>What level of hell am I in?</i>

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.930
H-Hey! Hey, you!

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:03.890
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.390
<i>I'm floating.</i>

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.150
<i>What kind of reaction was that?</i>

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.570
<i>Wait a second.</i>

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:24.080
<i>If I was put in a state of suspended animation in the storybook world...</i>

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:25.710
<i>That means...</i>

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.420
How long have you been here?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.750
How long? Three years.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:36.010
Can I borrow your body once?

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.840
You've got it on your face.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.520
<i>What's this atmosphere?</i>

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.020
<i>It's a shame since the manager's enjoying herself with my face,</i>

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.150
<i>but it's just pissing me off.</i>

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.530
I'll get the backpack.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:00.620
I'll go, too!

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:02.620
Um, actually...

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.330
I don't really want to

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.170
be left alone here...

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:17.630
<i>The manager is acting like a child.</i>

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.090
After I finally caught you...

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.100
Rokka.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.720
<i>Or that's how it looks, anyway...</i>

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.890
<i>Yet...</i>

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.270
It's okay.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.150
I promise I'll be right back.

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:34.110
I just have to pee.

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:41.030
<i>What's that face of mine saying?!</i>

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.420
It feels like it's been a long time.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:00.050
Whose fault is that?

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:02.800
You've got more energy than I imagined.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:04.640
Anyway,

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.930
I never thought you would actually lend me your body.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:10.440
You're a good guy.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.900
Maybe we should just leave things as they are.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.270
I think you're going to hell.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.150
Hell?

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:23.030
Actually, yeah.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.370
Might not be a bad idea.

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:28.910
You...

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.790
You use a guy's body to do whatever you like...

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:36.170
Just because you gave up on everything when you were alive, that doesn't excuse...

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:37.800
I never gave up on anything.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:40.550
That's why I'm here, right?

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.970
If it meant leaving her alone,

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.560
I'd just as soon take her with me.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:50.560
I don't like the sound of that.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.690
For example,

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.560
I could send Rokka to the afterlife,

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:00.740
then hand you the baton as your body got arrested.

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:02.570
Joking or not, knock it off.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:04.160
Anyway,

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:07.080
keep your promise.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.910
She can't forget about you, but I can't do anything about that.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:16.330
Even if she's like that the rest of her life,

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:20.260
I don't mind.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:27.510
I get it, not being able to accept someone's death and say goodbye.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:29.930
But you of all people should know this.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.890
You're...

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.810
never coming back, but she's taking great care

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:40.530
of the shop you left behind.

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:43.570
She took it all on herself.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.950
So stop

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.700
interfering with her.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:56.120
<i>Even though you're separated from your body, you're crying.</i>

00:16:57.920 --> 00:16:58.790
Shit...

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:02.130
<i>I suppose it's possible because the container is still alive.</i>

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.130
Why are you crying?

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:07.260
Shut up!

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.010
The rice ball...

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.390
I left it half-eaten.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.980
I'd like to get back to it...

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:18.270
Don't crave food with my body!

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:25.110
<i>Why does Hazuki have such strong feelings for Rokka?</i>

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:29.910
<i>Though if he asked me the same thing...</i>

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:32.740
<i>It's a stupid question.</i>

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.670
Sorry to keep you waiting, Rokka.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.250
You didn't eat while you were waiting?

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:46.050
Can I eat the last one?

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:49.260
Go ahead.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.180
Lucky me.

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:56.810
<i>Just the right thing</i>

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:58.980
<i>for a last supper.</i>

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.910
<i>In doing this,</i>

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.370
<i>I've become like the wind.</i>

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.080
<i>Like the air.</i>

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.080
<i>It feels weird not having a physical body.</i>

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.840
<i>Unbeknownst to anyone,</i>

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.720
<i>he spent three years like this.</i>

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.130
<i>A stalker.</i>

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.010
<i>Is that creepy?</i>

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.640
<i>Or admirable?</i>

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:39.640
<i>Two ways of looking at it.</i>

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:47.820
You're staring too much.

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:50.400
You'll burn a hole in me.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:55.280
Although it is for the last time...

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:01.210
You've had short hair for a long time now.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:04.960
This round head.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.050
It's beautiful.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.010
Shimao, how long have you...

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:11.430
Um...

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.640
The way you look now...

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.760
You're referring to the owner of this body?

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:19.140
Yes.

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.520
Is it really that important

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:23.600
how long it's been me?

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:25.650
No, but...

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:31.320
Yes.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:34.320
Sorry.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.790
It really is important.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:44.750
Until I came here and confirmed it,

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:48.050
I thought you were Hazuki the whole time.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.300
Well, of course.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:54.180
More than three years have passed since your funeral, Shimao,

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:59.470
but after Hazuki started working for me part-time,

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:02.850
all kinds of things got complicated.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.440
If I ask you a question, will you answer it?

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:08.820
As much as I'm able.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:11.320
<i>Acting all innocent...</i>

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:15.820
Were those presents in the shop from you, Shimao?

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:16.870
Yeah.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:18.620
<i>Presents?</i>

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.460
And you went with me to the sea?

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:24.290
Yeah.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.460
<i>The sea?</i>

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:31.960
Then Hazuki didn't spend the night with me at the inn.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.340
<i>What inn?</i>

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:41.560
<i>What did he do when I wasn't in control?!</i>

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:46.310
<i>But wait a second...</i>

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:51.480
<i>She thought it was me at the time.</i>

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:57.910
Then...

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:02.290
Then the Hazuki that I fell in love with...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.790
Where is...

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:13.010
he?

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:25.230
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:30.980
you always smile

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:35.070
Tell me why

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:38.950
it won't go away

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.740
I gave you everything

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:42.580
You gave me anything

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:47.370
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.040
still my everything

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:52.250
I love you

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:55.630
It is a miracle

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:58.760
like fleeting snow

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:04.720
that fell in summer

00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:11.730
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.940
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:22.450
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:28.120
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:35.170
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:40.300
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:44.310
you're right beside me
